  "conclusion": "Under two accepted simultaneous runs, Galaxy retained roughly 3.8-4.0k missing rVFC callbacks and 26-28 draw submits per second, while POCO retained 49-327 missing callbacks and 56-59 draw submits per second. This reproduces the large Galaxy-specific live Original rendering deficit under the fixed 60 Hz condition.",
  "limitations": [
    "rVFC missedCallbackFrames counts gaps in callback observation relative to the presentedFrames counter; it is not a direct count of physical display scanout drops.",
    "The two runs cover different ten-minute live broadcast intervals. Within each run the devices share the same live input interval; small differences between runs are not treatment effects.",
    "Galaxy was fixed at 60 Hz while POCO retained its normal OS setting, so this establishes user-visible device-condition scale rather than hardware-only causality.",
    "Physical scanout, pixel correctness, subjective picture quality, and audible A/V synchronization were not measured.",
    "Pre-sample trace drops are retained separately; measured-interval droppedEvents was zero and the validator accepted both runs.",
    "Source filesystem paths and LAN addresses are omitted; SHA-256 values retain traceability to the private archive."
  ]
